:db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74505/selection/ma-v1/d0faef89c35c19603f8581f83493ce4f01641b85c9423e32a735f2bca5e92b58/12b48b00f9c1ff14570ca66bc629787a88856efba1cda24cfb28da58c148801a" :answer/id #uuid "db8fe72f-b705-59fc-8d45-b48f66b2782b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "22" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74505/selection/ma-v1/d0faef89c35c19603f8581f83493ce4f01641b85c9423e32a735f2bca5e92b58/56c57502ed9362f3f416b4398e79545a0252f6594946b2d60ff940ea8bef1e7b" :answer/id #uuid "6766b3d5-12b3-5e26-8b8e-54ef00dae87b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "44" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74505/selection/ma-v1/d0faef89c35c19603f8581f83493ce4f01641b85c9423e32a735f2bca5e92b58" :answer-field/id #uuid "09e4d037-f7bd-52a1-9c0c-54175d1d1ee9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-74505/selection/ma-v1/d0faef89c35c19603f8581f83493ce4f01641b85c9423e32a735f2bca5e92b58/286fb92e9ba180b012d241bb7e762701483c9c864420d9df6597147f2e2fb458" :answer-field/choices ["q-74505/selection/ma-v1/d0faef89c35c19603f8581f83493ce4f01641b85c9423e32a735f2bca5e92b58/0fbe558572ecce67593db00d22f0d8d9d09c98d019451cd13488790a441e6c9c" "q-74505/selection/ma-v1/d0faef89c35c19603f8581f83493ce4f01641b85c9423e32a735f2bca5e92b58/286fb92e9ba180b012d241bb7e762701483c9c864420d9df6597147f2e2fb458" "q-74505/selection/ma-v1/d0faef89c35c19603f8581f83493ce4f01641b85c9423e32a735f2bca5e92b58/a20b3c9808c291c56ec5bfc5f0f93a856fc692714ca7ebd36c5e4bc361f7075c" "q-74505/selection/ma-v1/d0faef89c35c19603f8581f83493ce4f01641b85c9423e32a735f2bca5e92b58/12b48b00f9c1ff14570ca66bc629787a88856efba1cda24cfb28da58c148801a" "q-74505/selection/ma-v1/d0faef89c35c19603f8581f83493ce4f01641b85c9423e32a735f2bca5e92b58/56c57502ed9362f3f416b4398e79545a0252f6594946b2d60ff940ea8bef1e7b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-74505"] :question/worked-solution "In this case, we have $n=4$ rectangles. Using the left Riemann sum, the area is approximated as\n\n$$\nA≈f(2)Δ{x}_{1}+f(4)Δ{x}_{2}+f(8)Δ{x}_{3}+f(10)Δ{x}_{4},\n$$\n\nwhere each $Δ{x}_{i}$ is calculated by considering the step between a particular $x$-value and the next one, i.e.,\n\n$$\nΔ{x}_{i}={x}_{i+1}-{x}_{i}.\n$$\n\nWe set up a value table that includes the $Δx$'s.\n\n| $x$ | $2$ | $4$ | $8$ | $10$ | $12$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $Δx$ | $2$ | $4$ | $2$ | $2$ | $-$ |\n| $f(x)$ | $5$ | $3$ | $2$ | $1$ | $1$ |\n\nFinally, we plug in the numbers to approximate the area under the curve and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ≈5\\cdot 2+3\\cdot 4+2\\cdot 2+1\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =10+12+4+2 \\\\  & =28.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/answer-fields ["q-74505/selection/ma-v1/d0faef89c35c19603f8581f83493ce4f01641b85c9423e32a735f2bca5e92b58"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-117278/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "b87a0cd5-ed42-5831-8b73-6ef14d1fe940" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117278/selection/df7c1a7c7ba551e4cac0fd39a3958b5b0ab3088597abd7b4a39c505b31931fad" :answer/id #uuid "e352e279-23cc-5fd6-a6f9-5c667b866ab0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2-\\operatorname{cos}⁡1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117278/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "622002d4-df72-5060-b2ac-6b231db87adc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117278/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "87f994a6-39cb-592b-ad83-8b7228910a6e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117278/selection/1d58d34b893282f6079d82f1d5604b758d6807794b9391a226c60e4c851b9f7b" :answer/id #uuid "08dad672-a923-542a-b2a4-8075d5a00c84" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\operatorname{cos}⁡1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117278/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "eb530fa1-c008-55fc-925b-31d688efd41d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-117278/selection/1d58d34b893282f6079d82f1d5604b758d6807794b9391a226c60e4c851b9f7b" :answer-field/choices ["q-117278/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-117278/selection/df7c1a7c7ba551e4cac0fd39a3958b5b0ab3088597abd7b4a39c505b31931fad" "q-117278/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-117278/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" "q-117278/selection/1d58d34b893282f6079d82f1d5604b758d6807794b9391a226c60e4c851b9f7b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-117278" :question/id #uuid "e902d8d9-f9a5-5a6b-9ee4-5e36cb9511d0" :question/math-academy-id "q-117278" :question/problem "Find ${f}^{′}(1)$ if $f(x)={\\int }_{-{x}^{3}}^{x}{t}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t.$" :question/worked-solution "Here, both the lower and upper limits contain a variable. However, to apply FTC II, we need the variable to be on the upper limit only. So, we can split the integral into two integrals, and rewrite them so that in both cases the variable is on the upper limit. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-{x}^{3}}^{x}{t}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{-{x}^{3}}^{a}{t}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{a}^{x}{t}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{a}^{-{x}^{3}}{t}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{a}^{x}{t}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ is any constant number between $-{x}^{3}$ and $x.$\n\nThe integrand ${t}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t$ is continuous for all $t,$ so applying the FTC II gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-{\\int }_{a}^{-{x}^{3}}{t}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{a}^{x}{t}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({\\int }_{a}^{-{x}^{3}}{t}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({\\int }_{a}^{x}{t}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}({\\int }_{a}^{u}{t}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t)+{x}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\  & =-(-3{x}^{2}){u}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡u+{x}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\  & =3{x}^{2}{(-{x}^{3})}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-{x}^{3})+{x}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\  & =3{x}^{14}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{x}^{3}+{x}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we used the substitution $u=-{x}^{3}.$\n\nFinally, we can compute ${f}^{′}(1).$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(1) & =3(1)^{14}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{1}^{3}+{1}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡1 \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{cos}⁡1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡1 \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{cos}⁡1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-117278/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a0f285ec-4f37-5d0d-a65c-be3ca48c740f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-117278"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-124842/selection/a7d4572ad2034a50d8eb4976eb2ac98502990bf5044acfafca2609825eb1a707" :answer/id #uuid "afe5eea0-595e-5ea2-9acf-4f8456f5ae5b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The series converges by the comparison test" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124842/selection/fc609679185a575714f001f59b259be06dfeec6233260d222db62bb48c88604b" :answer/id #uuid "7ce831fa-614a-5c58-9a2e-16a4ef99b4ff" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The series is a divergent $p$-series" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124842/selection/072d7646bcfb9a6b4d003603f274bf71733aef10cd7dfde3102a44f56ff8a108" :answer/id #uuid "92d3802d-12da-56ba-a1a7-d51ab729bdee" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The series is a convergent $p$-series" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124842/selection/e6481344e45d1a8a27277bd5359523ea8171e2afe5acb5646cdcbefa5a9a4cd6" :answer/id #uuid "fc60143a-cd43-5321-bac4-7d1a8d98affa" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The series diverges by the comparison test" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124842/selection/7b10227501f7a5579189e3b959f2550f09184e9b6a53ba28e5f5dc65e30be217" :answer/id #uuid "f02d658b-1a6e-5de6-9f6f-6d6e4484bdcd" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The series diverges because $\\frac{{n}^{3}+3\\sqrt{n}}{2{n}^{4}}\\to 0$ as $n\\to \\infty $" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124842/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "830e1edc-93f2-59dc-98b1-8dfed00ee40f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-124842/selection/e6481344e45d1a8a27277bd5359523ea8171e2afe5acb5646cdcbefa5a9a4cd6" :answer-field/choices ["q-124842/selection/a7d4572ad2034a50d8eb4976eb2ac98502990bf5044acfafca2609825eb1a707" "q-124842/selection/fc609679185a575714f001f59b259be06dfeec6233260d222db62bb48c88604b" "q-124842/selection/072d7646bcfb9a6b4d003603f274bf71733aef10cd7dfde3102a44f56ff8a108" "q-124842/selection/e6481344e45d1a8a27277bd5359523ea8171e2afe5acb5646cdcbefa5a9a4cd6" "q-124842/selection/7b10227501f7a5579189e3b959f2550f09184e9b6a53ba28e5f5dc65e30be217"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-124842" :question/id #uuid "65e12f07-0da8-512d-aa8f-71eff1375d5e" :question/math-academy-id "q-124842" :question/problem "Given the series $S={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{{n}^{3}+3\\sqrt{n}}{2{n}^{4}},$ which of the following is true?" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that $S$ is not a $p$-series, and we know from the $n$th term test the condition $\\frac{{n}^{3}+3\\sqrt{n}}{2{n}^{4}}\\to 0$ as $n\\to \\infty $ as $n\\to \\infty $ does not tell us anything about the convergence or divergence of the series.\n\nThe comparison test for divergence states the following:\n\n*Consider two series ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}$ and ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}$ such that ${a}_{n}$ and ${b}_{n}$ are both positive and ${a}_{n}\\ge {b}_{n}$ for all $n.$ If ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}$ is divergent, then ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}$ is also divergent.*\n\nWe follow four steps to show that $S$ is divergent.\n\n**Step 1**: First, we let ${a}_{n}=\\frac{{n}^{3}+3\\sqrt{n}}{2{n}^{4}}$ and ${b}_{n}=\\frac{1}{2n}.$ We note that ${a}_{n}>0$ and ${b}_{n}>0$ for all $n\\ge 1.$\n\n**Step 2**: We show that ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}$ is divergent. We have,\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}=\\frac{1}{2}{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{n}\n$$\n\nwhich is divergent by the $p$-series test.\n\n**Step 3**: We show that ${a}_{n}\\ge {b}_{n}$ for all $n\\ge 1.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & \\overset{?}{\\ge }{b}_{n} \\\\ \\frac{{n}^{3}+3\\sqrt{n}}{2{n}^{4}} & \\ge \\frac{{n}^{3}}{2{n}^{4}}=\\frac{1}{2n}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 4**: We conclude that ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}$ is divergent by the comparison test." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-124842/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4778fcea-d30f-5482-9285-ad36315170c7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-124842"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-339145/field-1/077e9e54179703601a4dd3177dbc11815994aa839a7d7d5b12c3e1ec39527ef2" :answer/id #uuid "2fda18aa-1a14-51d2-8bcc-7f9ebda84856" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{12x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339145/field-1/3341f139f0ee0d62d8758bd01e1eedd529e55f6b927830ec42423f0a16d137a0" :answer/id #uuid "553c56bb-0776-5a1f-b5d2-9a856c8091b2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339145/field-1/192c6030d8816553cdfcf13c7f5f26bd0bc0f29788b453b1e64332880bc35044" :answer/id #uuid "5597871a-edaf-5f10-ba47-78d49a5116c2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339145/field-1/8d5d023c3a301fb9a8d23477feea46f05f0d5405aee5f9b110d5b86d86e2e4dd" :answer/id #uuid "1d12cb43-99f4-5b54-bd11-9c5ed6be9073" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{{x}^{2}/12}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339145/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "4b8ce280-64e4-5b33-aca1-5b011968bfff" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-339145/field-1/8d5d023c3a301fb9a8d23477feea46f05f0d5405aee5f9b110d5b86d86e2e4dd" :answer-field/choices ["q-339145/field-1/077e9e54179703601a4dd3177dbc11815994aa839a7d7d5b12c3e1ec39527ef2" "q-339145/field-1/3341f139f0ee0d62d8758bd01e1eedd529e55f6b927830ec42423f0a16d137a0" "q-339145/field-1/192c6030d8816553cdfcf13c7f5f26bd0bc0f29788b453b1e64332880bc35044" "q-339145/field-1/8d5d023c3a301fb9a8d23477feea46f05f0d5405aee5f9b110d5b86d86e2e4dd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-339145/field-2/ccfdfe1553bd07a74184fa884521de80a6a997a2cb3a9bc67957d68dfb3f0e82" :answer/id #uuid "54b038d8-eb0d-5f7a-badd-7ee99b7ac1b4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{6{x}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339145/field-2/f44fb6925196a9ad9c5e370efad7055bfa4d3b57f6e8601730e9bc6f87e27b21" :answer/id #uuid "8be3aed3-7040-5b8d-9741-df687946852a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6-{e}^{-{x}^{2}/12}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339145/field-2/ecdf59a6922e0a715d091f39d1edb555e71827b1cef672bec6f966d7329a486d" :answer/id #uuid "91ca2193-058c-5514-989f-b0f6d9e74e61" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6{x}^{2}+5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339145/field-2/61b414f03fb19f29a438aafd2c26809ce879d88ba614d981b6366b238a05ca82" :answer/id #uuid "b2a3b009-67bb-5628-bb7b-390289527147" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6x+5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339145/field-2/3106d29ec84ff4a540fd8dad587c31084ffb5bcb597f43d1abcf43548fc86090" :answer/id #uuid "45b7b187-72c2-558b-b7d8-483c8c41df13" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6-{e}^{{x}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339145/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "3333afe3-58ca-50c1-b6a5-292fad2e514a" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-339145/field-2/f44fb6925196a9ad9c5e370efad7055bfa4d3b57f6e8601730e9bc6f87e27b21" :answer-field/choices ["q-339145/field-2/ccfdfe1553bd07a74184fa884521de80a6a997a2cb3a9bc67957d68dfb3f0e82" "q-339145/field-2/f44fb6925196a9ad9c5e370efad7055bfa4d3b57f6e8601730e9bc6f87e27b21" "q-339145/field-2/ecdf59a6922e0a715d091f39d1edb555e71827b1cef672bec6f966d7329a486d" "q-339145/field-2/61b414f03fb19f29a438aafd2c26809ce879d88ba614d981b6366b238a05ca82" "q-339145/field-2/3106d29ec84ff4a540fd8dad587c31084ffb5bcb597f43d1abcf43548fc86090"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-339145" :question/id #uuid "b18cb65d-b781-5075-91bf-6c656ac3ed30" :question/math-academy-id "q-339145" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{x}{6}y=x,\\,y(0)=5\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below.\n$\\,$ An integrating factor for this equation is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The solution to the initial value problem is $y(x)=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x),\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=\\frac{x}{6}$ and $Q(x)=x.$\n\nWe compute an integrating factor using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (x/6)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{{x}^{2}/12}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the equation in standard form by $I(x)={e}^{{x}^{2}/12}$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{{x}^{2}/12}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{x}{6}y) & ={e}^{{x}^{2}/12}\\cdot x \\\\ {e}^{{x}^{2}/12}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{x}{6}{e}^{{x}^{2}/12}\\cdot y & =x{e}^{{x}^{2}/12} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{e}^{{x}^{2}/12}) & =x{e}^{{x}^{2}/12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x,$ making use of the substitution $u=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{12}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{e}^{{x}^{2}/12})\\text{d}x & =\\int x{e}^{{x}^{2}/12}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{e}^{{x}^{2}/12} & =\\int 6{e}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ y{e}^{{x}^{2}/12} & =6{e}^{u}+C \\\\ y{e}^{{x}^{2}/12} & =6{e}^{{x}^{2}/12}+C \\\\ y & =6+C{e}^{-{x}^{2}/12}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the general solution. To find the value of $C$ corresponding to the specific solution, we apply the initial condition $y(0)=5$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =6+C{e}^{-{0}^{2}/12} \\\\ 5 & =6+C \\\\ C & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=6-{e}^{-{x}^{2}/12}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-339145/field-1" "q-339145/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "01c5809f-cb10-5192-b646-13036813137d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-339145"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-90693/selection/d0acfd61e76f4e6caf3700151d55ed6b85d31e18512f1f829e15334b646cf432" :answer/id #uuid "941c8fcd-64af-5b8b-af8b-f334e03514b0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=x\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90693/selection/2753f629e5324886966eb64c4e3cbf5eca489cdf125f9fb13b77ff7880644792" :answer/id #uuid "73d46a52-c720-5be4-bc0d-36ed1a930c5e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C{x}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90693/selection/a9744be0efde462e6771700bb3a7c86e99259c06b3197e746b5c59b205ff746b" :answer/id #uuid "b5013620-85cf-596c-a1fc-5a58e3f4a66a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=x\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+Cx" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90693/selection/42ff65d80346d6f2e04f6280cdfd841540db021cff3161d0030086002eddebaa" :answer/id #uuid "9b167bc2-b2b5-58dd-9241-fa6cd6b3ff0e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+Cx" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90693/selection/806ab4aa0224366748949a9d0e15861d4c45c1c657762c2deeab1d88f7c9696e" :answer/id #uuid "92e86c9b-2d2e-5779-9135-add724e60455" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C{x}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90693/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "bf385671-f58b-559d-b2cc-f06901fe762b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-90693/selection/a9744be0efde462e6771700bb3a7c86e99259c06b3197e746b5c59b205ff746b" :answer-field/choices ["q-90693/selection/d0acfd61e76f4e6caf3700151d55ed6b85d31e18512f1f829e15334b646cf432" "q-90693/selection/2753f629e5324886966eb64c4e3cbf5eca489cdf125f9fb13b77ff7880644792" "q-90693/selection/a9744be0efde462e6771700bb3a7c86e99259c06b3197e746b5c59b205ff746b" "q-90693/selection/42ff65d80346d6f2e04f6280cdfd841540db021cff3161d0030086002eddebaa" "q-90693/selection/806ab4aa0224366748949a9d0e15861d4c45c1c657762c2deeab1d88f7c9696e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-90693" :question/id #uuid "06efe7ad-4702-5be5-a0d4-8b7bf053efc8" :question/math-academy-id "q-90693" :question/problem "Use the transformation $y=v(x)x$ to find the general solution of the following homogeneous differential equation.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{x+y}{x}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "With $y=v(x)x$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x) \\\\  & =x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{x+y}{x} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\frac{x+(vx)}{x} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\frac{x(1+v)}{x} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =1+v \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating both sides with respect to $x$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\,\\text{d}v & =\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ v & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the transformation $y=vx$, we get\n\n$$\nv=\\frac{y}{x}\\,.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our solution, we finally obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{y}{x} & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C \\\\ y & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+Cx.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-90693/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "49eaf082-07de-5468-a2d7-4cdfce27a553"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-90693"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-90806/selection/33eb89a54eb765b238803b92e8939ffed1bbc7bf144d50c21da7d5fd439f77fb" :answer/id #uuid "3c5f8833-71b2-5732-8bdc-8971df32c24e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5{e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90806/selection/bc171605b3aa1d7bf7c68bfc6039adcbc6bb14d5e8343ae904792da6189fd94d" :answer/id #uuid "92a4053d-2962-515b-afbb-342b22f6dc13" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{e}^{-2x}+{e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90806/selection/52791cd22837017b744072330ba9b67613d1f7eb020c1de05e165671fcaf2b57" :answer/id #uuid "5b72d5e2-f8a8-5930-8ab4-699196c518a1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2{e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90806/selection/07146cd7ba6b70243834588c57eb5deef851d85fe0bdf3b64a88f63f8ff165e8" :answer/id #uuid "de1070ff-56b0-5e34-85cf-c6d843d281de" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x-3{e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90806/selection/140593c07e18c19e2b9df6a13fe987702a245cb6dde43e11a676f89b0a543f6a" :answer/id #uuid "5a819b6b-ec52-540d-9ab8-f79a67b2b962" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3{e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x-8{e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90806/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f0642fc6-3837-59f6-8f8c-ed9e523144d1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-90806/selection/bc171605b3aa1d7bf7c68bfc6039adcbc6bb14d5e8343ae904792da6189fd94d" :answer-field/choices ["q-90806/selection/33eb89a54eb765b238803b92e8939ffed1bbc7bf144d50c21da7d5fd439f77fb" "q-90806/selection/bc171605b3aa1d7bf7c68bfc6039adcbc6bb14d5e8343ae904792da6189fd94d" "q-90806/selection/52791cd22837017b744072330ba9b67613d1f7eb020c1de05e165671fcaf2b57" "q-90806/selection/07146cd7ba6b70243834588c57eb5deef851d85fe0bdf3b64a88f63f8ff165e8" "q-90806/selection/140593c07e18c19e2b9df6a13fe987702a245cb6dde43e11a676f89b0a543f6a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-90806" :question/id #uuid "3b23b2eb-59fb-5302-951a-3f3e5716ee74" :question/math-academy-id "q-90806" :question/problem "Given that $y=y(x)$ satisfies the equation ${y}^{″}+4{y}^{′}+20y=0,$ which of the following is **not** a solution to this equation?" :question/worked-solution "Assuming $y={e}^{\\lambda x}$ and differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x},\\,{y}^{″}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}+4\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x}+20{e}^{\\lambda x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda x}({\\lambda }^{2}+4\\lambda +20) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }^{2}+4\\lambda +20=0.\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation can be solved by completing the square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+4\\lambda +20 & =0 \\\\ ({\\lambda }^{2}+4\\lambda +4)-4+20 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +2)^{2}+16 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +2)^{2} & =-16 \\\\ \\lambda +2 & =\\pm 4\\text{i} \\\\ \\lambda  & =-2\\pm 4\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $\\lambda =-2\\pm 4\\text{i}$ are the complex roots of the auxiliary equation.\n\nThus, any linear combination of the functions $\\text{Re}({e}^{(-2+4\\text{i})x})={e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x$ and $\\text{Im}({e}^{(-2+4\\text{i})x})={e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x$ is a solution to the original differential equation. \n\nAmong the given options, only $4{e}^{-2x}+{e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x$ is not a solution." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-90806/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "092a6c8c-7bea-5c53-88ac-f5dc8b16c357"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-90806"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186260488 :question/answer-fields 17592186260489] {:db/id "q-47447/selection/ma-v1/bced79e027f92b1c553aa4a820ef0640636c91f0287786ab952a0acf2a522b97/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "0c7ba49c-4a26-54e2-bd75-42ad05f3b4cb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-47447/selection/ma-v1/bced79e027f92b1c553aa4a820ef0640636c91f0287786ab952a0acf2a522b97/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "9075ff78-741a-5729-812d-2a80fd97eb3f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-47447/selection/ma-v1/bced79e027f92b1c553aa4a820ef0640636c91f0287786ab952a0acf2a522b97/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "04abffd8-7053-53e6-b817-84082d046c33" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/v