ure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343302/field-3/08fc3946806b1a30042891f2e1a7c0b3d141b9fbc3c3f65ca96eb5887fe978cb" :answer/id #uuid "d417faed-38a1-5dca-a375-e4508e2e18e1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$W(x)\\ne 0$ for all $x\\in R$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343302/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "69f067df-2c92-5450-9de2-4a884870ae7f" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-343302/field-3/08fc3946806b1a30042891f2e1a7c0b3d141b9fbc3c3f65ca96eb5887fe978cb" :answer-field/choices ["q-343302/field-3/e3cf2efbe1b243991dad4797fc800da87c7458d44af17da132ec499bd6595b28" "q-343302/field-3/d2f4a8d7bf19ba91ffcfe3f2bf391cb2285df557a172f4d58a990c4e894ee1e1" "q-343302/field-3/08fc3946806b1a30042891f2e1a7c0b3d141b9fbc3c3f65ca96eb5887fe978cb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-343302" :question/id #uuid "736a842a-a005-5f7c-a75f-80d3e3e641b7" :question/math-academy-id "q-343302" :question/problem "$$\n{y}^{″}+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+1}{y}^{′}+Q(x)y=0\n$$\n\nLet ${y}_{1}$ and ${y}_{2}$ be solutions to the second-order homogeneous differential equation above, where $Q(x)$ is continuous on $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ The Wronskian satisfies $W(0)=2.$ Select the correct options in the reasoning below.\nThe Wronskian $W(x)$ satisfies the following first-order differential equation:\n\n$$\n-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+1}\n$$\n\nSolving this equation, we get\n\n$$\nC{e}^{\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x)}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nNow, using the fact that $W(0)=2,$ we obtain \n{{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "Abel's identity says that if ${y}_{1}$ and ${y}_{2}$ are solutions of\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+P(x){y}^{′}+Q(x)y=0,\n$$\n\nthen their Wronskian $W(x)$ satisfies\n\n$$\n{W}^{′}(x)=-P(x)W(x).\n$$\n\nIn our equation, the coefficient of ${y}^{′}$ is \n\n$$\nP(x)=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+1}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting into Abel's identity gives\n\n$$\n{W}^{′}(x)=-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+1}W(x).\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the first-order differential equation for $W:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{W}^{′} & =-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+1}W \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}W}{W} & =-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+1}\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{\\text{d}W}{W} & =\\int -\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|W| & =-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x)+K \\\\ |W| & ={e}^{K}{e}^{-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x)} \\\\ W & =C{e}^{-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant.\n\nNext, we use the given value $W(0)=2$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}W(0) & =C{e}^{-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(0)} \\\\ 2 & =C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have $W(x)\\ne 0\\text{ for all }x\\in R.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-343302/field-1" "q-343302/field-2" "q-343302/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "734fe467-57d6-5b3f-a61e-1e2e4624b5fc"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-343302"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-331821/field-1/b2113f87c6b6bf1c28ed979a0b201698e58e7d96097115d9adad15dc8952f22c" :answer/id #uuid "68ca7452-35a7-52eb-ac91-9c85bdeb664f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{-st}\\cdot {e}^{-t}b(t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-331821/field-1/01bab06769e694adb3a060851042973e55b2c27f612b5aa8251e45ca715e3c92" :answer/id #uuid "bbf7f5f6-b3eb-5e96-b6b2-0fda4155754c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{st}\\cdot {e}^{t}b(t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-331821/field-1/704d7733985fc7a6983ed411516c0a8990795e2e7d164b2db41ae5e37a262d13" :answer/id #uuid "cf56f66e-7e38-576f-8b52-54d0b1dda3ae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{st}\\cdot {e}^{-t}b(t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-331821/field-1/00bd56bdc329d845ccbd1a3876a47676803b97a93ecc2aee6f8558b0a92f0749" :answer/id #uuid "5b60c69c-0c76-58c4-9eb9-04820c36b449" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{-st}\\cdot {e}^{t}b(t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/i